{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Each man according to his dream</b> — according to the dream and related to its matter; this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 41:12). But it is more correct to say that he means: each one of us he interpreted exactly as the true outcome of his dream that would come to him, for as he interpreted, so it was for us. And similarly (Genesis 49:28), <b>\"each according to his blessing he blessed them\"</b> — according to the blessing that would come to him. But in my opinion this is unnecessary; rather, he said: \"each his dream he interpreted to us,\" and \"it was as he interpreted\" — to each one so it came and reached us. He stated that they were different dreams with different interpretations, as he would explain, so that one should not think that both of them dreamed one dream with one interpretation for both. And similarly, in my opinion, <b>\"each according to his blessing he blessed\"</b> — that he did not bless them with one identical blessing for all, but a distinct blessing for each one, as he explained and said to him:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:42:49.990781815Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}